The Fortran sources in src/bhmiepy/_fortran/ (bhmie.f90, types.f90) are copies
of files from that repository, snapshot taken at upstream commit
37c072909a67d1027120762680a1c0b350875398 (2013-10-08), and may be modified for
bhmiepy; any modifications are recorded in the header of each file. A pristine
copy of the upstream tree is kept in the top-level bhmie/ directory of this
repository for reference and testing.

The underlying BHMIE subroutine is derived from the Mie scattering program in
Appendix A of:

  C. F. Bohren and D. R. Huffman, "Absorption and Scattering of Light by
  Small Particles" (Wiley, 1983)

with extensive modifications by B. T. Draine (Princeton University
Observatory), as documented in the history log of bhmie/original/bhmie.f in
the upstream snapshot.

---

src/bhmiepy/_loglog.py is a Python translation (derivative work) of
algorithms from:

  fortranlib — https://github.com/astrofrog/fortranlib
  Copyright (c) 2009-13, Thomas P. Robitaille
  Distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
  See LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause-fortranlib.txt.

The translated routines (integral_loglog, interp1d_loglog, locate, logspace,
and their helper formulas) define the numerical conventions the upstream
bhmie dust pipeline is built on; they are reproduced operation by operation
so that bhmiepy's results match the upstream tool.
